&lt;p&gt;To determine which Object Class your anomaly falls under, you can apply the &#039;Locked Box Test&#039;. If the anomaly were locked in a box, would it be contained?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If yes, the anomaly is &lt;strong&gt;Safe&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If yes (but it would need to be checked on), the anomaly is &lt;strong&gt;Euclid&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If not, the anomaly is &lt;strong&gt;Keter&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If the anomaly &lt;em&gt;itself&lt;/em&gt; is used to contain other anomalies (or otherwise help the Foundation), the anomaly is &lt;strong&gt;Thaumiel&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
