&lt;li&gt;Procedures are written as things which either currently &lt;em&gt;are&lt;/em&gt; being done or &lt;em&gt;are &lt;strong&gt;to be&lt;/strong&gt; done&lt;/em&gt; (&amp;quot;object &lt;em&gt;is&lt;/em&gt; kept in a cell&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;object &lt;em&gt;is &lt;strong&gt;to be&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt; kept in a cell&amp;quot;). &#039;Must&#039;, &#039;shall be&#039;, &#039;should&#039;, or &#039;would&#039; are typically not used.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Procedures should be brief, clear, and succinct &amp;#8212; but interesting enough to be memorable.&lt;/li&gt;
